L000442	{\it Discussions.}--
L000443	For the carbon target data, the $P_{\gamma \gamma}$ dependence of the observed enhancement was examined more precisely using the fitting model with the signal function simulated with $k_1=0.06$.
L000444	Figure~\ref{pdep} shows the yield ratio of the signal component $N_{\mathrm{sig}}$ to the $\eta^\prime$ decays in vacuum $N_{\mathrm{vac}}$ for the different requirements of $P_{\gamma \gamma} < P_{\mathrm{cut}}$.
L000445	Although the statistical uncertainty is large, the measured ratio increases by selecting lower $P_{\gamma \gamma}$ events.
L000446	The $P_{\gamma \gamma}$ dependence is similar between the measurement and the expectation from the simulation of in-medium $\eta^\prime$ mass reduction, as shown by the dashed line.
L000447	This line was obtained by a fit of the simulation result (solid line) with a scale factor of $14.3$.
L000448	The need for a scale factor implies the possibility of the partial $\gamma \gamma$ decay width variation inside a nucleus \cite{MUTO2007}.
L000449	Such a change may be partly explained by the medium modification of the $\eta^\prime$ wave function \cite{10.1093/ptep/ptu023}.
L000450	
L000451	In the spectral fit with the simulated signal function, the total decay width parameter $k_2$ was fixed to $105$.
L000452	Even if $k_2$ was varied from $50$ to $500$, the most probable $k_1$ value remained unchanged while showing a large uncertainty for $k_2$.
L000453	From Eq.~\ref{eq:1}, the measured $k_1$ value corresponds to the $\etap$ mass reduction of $57.5^{+~5.7}_{-27.8}$~$\mathrm{MeV/c^2}$ at the normal nuclear density.
L000454	It matches a lower range of the current theoretical predictions.
L000455	In addition, it does not contradict the previous results of the search for $\etap$ mesic nuclei \cite{YKTANAKA2018,TOMIDA2020}.
L000456	
L000457	
L000458	{\it Conclusions.}--
L000459	The present analysis searched for the in-medium mass spectral change of the $\eta^\prime$ meson, which was photoproduced using a carbon target and was detected through the $\gamma \gamma$ decay channel.
L000460	In the fit using the spectra of known processes, an enhancement was observed in the lower tail of the $\eta^\prime$ mass peak only when requiring $P_{\gamma \gamma} < 1$~$\mathrm{GeV/c}$.
L000461	Its significance was $4.7 \sigma$ by a fit excluding the excessive region.
L000462	In another spectral fit together with a simulated signal function, the best fit was obtained at $k_1 = 0.06^{+0.006}_{-0.029}$, indicating the significance of $4.1 \sigma$ (conservatively $3.7 \sigma$) based on the $\chi^2$ difference test.
L000463	The measured $k_1$ value corresponds to a mass reduction of $57.5^{+~5.7}_{-27.8}$~$\mathrm{MeV}/c^{2}$ at the normal nuclear density.
L000464	The present result is the first evidence of the spectral change in the direct measurement of the in-medium $\eta^\prime$ mass.\\
